# Next.js + TypeScript Conventions

## App Router boundaries

- Keep server logic in server contexts (`app/*` server components, route handlers, middleware).
- Add `"use client"` only when interactivity is required.
- Do not access browser APIs from server components.

## Supabase usage

- Use `lib/supabase/server.ts` in server contexts and `lib/supabase/client.ts` in client contexts.
- Keep auth/session flow consistent with existing callback and middleware implementation.
- Prefer explicit null/error handling for Supabase responses; avoid non-null assumptions on data.

## Type and state quality

- Avoid `any`; model external data with explicit types.
- Keep components focused and small; extract reusable UI/state logic into hooks or helpers.
- Validate user input at boundaries (forms, query params, external responses).

## UX and failure behavior

- Show actionable error messages for auth, booking, and profile update failures.
- Preserve loading and empty states for async pages/components.
